\pard\plain \tx0\tx360\tx720\tx1080\tx1440\tx1800\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\fi360\ltrch\loch {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Catalyst}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\pard\plain \sa180\sb180\ltrch\loch {Eddie slouched in the hard-backed chair, one boot tapping restlessly against the polished stone floor of the council building\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s. The air smelled of dust and cigarette smokes. Candidates sat in neat rows along the wall, each dressed as if this were some grand occasion. Tunics pressed, boots shined, even a whiff of cologne or two drifting through the air. Eddie wore the same work shirt he\u8217\'92d pulled on that morning, the sleeves rolled up and stained faintly with salt from Weshaven\u8217\'92s sea breeze.}
\par\plain {Markus had insisted this was a good idea. }{\f0\fs24\i1 \loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\af1\uc1\u8220\'93Alchemy Assistant. You know the stuff, don\u8217\'92t you? Just try. Worst case, you walk out with a few silvers for your time.\u8221\'94}{ Easy for Markus to say\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 he wasn\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t the one about to be paraded in front of council clerks who actually believed in this kind of work.}
\par\plain {Eddie leaned back, staring at the cracked ceiling tiles. He knew Alchemy well enough; he\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92d grown up around it. But that didn\u8217\'92t mean he wanted to sit here proving it like some eager apprentice. His stomach churned at the thought of showing them tricks he\u8217\'92d rather keep buried, transformations that never seemed to go quite the way he intended.}
\par\plain {A clerk shuffled past the candidates with a clipboard, ticking names off in brisk strokes of ink. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Edward Welton?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {Eddie straightened, rubbing the back of his neck. Boredom flickered into something sharper\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 reluctance edging on dread. He forced himself to his feet, already wishing Markus had kept his bright ideas to himself.}
\par\plain {The chamber was smaller than Eddie expected, paneled in dark wood and lit by a single oil chandelier that cast long, swaying shadows across the table. Three figures sat behind it.}
\par\plain {On the right, Mayor Holling puffed lazily at a pipe, the sweet-sour smell of smoke curling in the air. His eyes barely lifted when Eddie walked in, as though this whole ordeal were an inconvenience. To the left, Secretary Brann fussed with his papers, spectacles sliding down his nose. His quill scratched faintly, recording things Eddie couldn\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t see.}
\par\plain {But in the middle\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 where the attention ought to rest\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 sat someone Eddie didn\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t recognize.}
\par\plain {Her crimson coat caught the light, embroidered with curling threads of gold that seemed almost alive against the black cloak beneath. Her skin was a shade darker than most folk in Weshaven, and her hair, tied neatly back, gleamed like the flesh of a ripe apple. But what stopped Eddie mid-step were her ears. Long. Elegant. Unmistakable.}
\par\plain {An elf.}
\par\plain {He\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92d read about them, of course. Everyone had. Old Solivian tales painted them as proud, vanished rulers of the continent. But to see one here, in the council chamber of a fishing town\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 }
\par\plain {\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Sit down.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {Her voice was sharp, commanding, yet not unkind. Eddie realized he\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92d been staring. He blinked, tore his eyes away, and lowered himself into the chair opposite her. The wooden legs creaked louder than he would have liked.}
\par\plain {His pulse was quicker now, a stubborn reminder that this was not the routine interview Markus had promised.}
\par\plain {The elf tapped the parchment once with a slender finger, then set it aside. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Theory can be written about anyone,\u8221\'94 she said evenly. \u8220\'93But what matters is application. So tell me this, Edward\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \u8221\'94 her long ears twitched slightly as she leaned forward, \u8220\'93\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 if there were a fissure beneath this town, a hole in the ground leaking dangerous chemicals into the soil, what would you do to stop it?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {Eddie blinked. For a moment his mind went blank, the weight of her gaze pressing against him. Then, slowly, the part of him that Markus always accused of being }{\f0\fs24\i1 too bookish}{ clicked into place.}
\par\plain {\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93If I wanted to seal it up,\u8221\'94 he began carefully, \u8220\'93I couldn\u8217\'92t just plug the hole. It would just push through somewhere else. The ground around it would have to be reinforced so the toxins wouldn\u8217\'92t find another way out.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {The secretary paused mid-scribble, and even Mayor Holling\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s pipe stopped puffing. The elf gestured for him to continue.}
\par\plain {\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93There\u8217\'92s a technique,\u8221\'94 Eddie said, his voice steadier now, \u8220\'93called Cementation. It uses what\u8217\'92s already in the soil. Dissolved minerals in groundwater\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 calcite, silica, sometimes iron oxides\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 seep into compacted dirt. Over time, they precipitate, crystallizing out of the water and binding the soil particles together. They act like a natural glue, hardening the structure.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {He lifted his hands unconsciously, as though sketching the process in the air. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93But to make it effective, you\u8217\'92d need to accelerate it. Pressurize the seepage. That\u8217\'92s what turns mud into something closer to shale\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 dense, impermeable, and able to trap what\u8217\'92s beneath it.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {When he stopped, the silence returned. Eddie realized he\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92d been leaning forward, speaking faster than he intended, as if trying to outrun his own reluctance. Heat crept into his neck.}
\par\plain {The elf\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s crimson sleeve brushed the parchment as she folded her hands. She regarded him without expression, but her eyes\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 sharp and unreadable\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 lingered on him a fraction longer than comfort allowed.}}